Package: proselign
# Pure Python, but restricted to the architectures the local LLM stack it
# drives supports.  amd64 and arm64: full support (GPU builds of llama.cpp
# and vLLM, Ollama).  ppc64el and s390x: CPU-only tier (llama.cpp and the vLLM
# CPU backend; no Ollama, no GPU; s390x needs big-endian GGUF models).
Architecture: amd64 arm64 ppc64el s390x
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.10)
Suggests: llama.cpp | ollama
Description: learn a writer's prose style and align text to it, locally
 Proselign is a Unix filter that learns an individual author's
 characteristic prose style from a corpus of their documents and rewrites
 new text in that style, while preserving facts, figures, names, URLs,
 citations, quotations and Markdown structure.
 .
   cat draft.md | proselign --voice Bryan > final.md
 .
 It is local-first: voices are stored under $XDG_DATA_HOME, inference runs
 against a locally served model through any OpenAI-compatible endpoint
 (llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama), and nothing leaves the machine by default.
 The program itself has no dependencies beyond the Python standard library.
